  "audio": "026.hard-sandboxes-protect.mp3",
  "paragraph": 26,
  "text": "Hard sandboxes protect the machine, while tiered permissions protect human trust without slowing the agent to a crawl. Strong harnesses split every action into three clear tiers. Tier one covers read-only tools like grep, file reads, and git status, which run silently with zero friction. Tier two covers scoped workspace edits and local test runs allowed automatically inside the sandbox policy. Tier three covers destructive, external, or production actions like git push, database writes, or deleting files. For those operations, the harness pauses and waits for explicit human approval before running.",
